    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="0808" n="794" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg794"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.76 Monitoring/500: Airgram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-02-05T18:30:00-04:00">February 5, 1943—6:30
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–378. Your 70, January 13, noon.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d659-f1"/> Department
                    entirely agreeable that S. R. Lines, Federal Communications Commission engineer
                    who is now in Venezuela shall serve as instructor to Venezuelan technicians in
                    direction finder project for elimination of clandestine radio stations. He will
                    probably remain in Venezuela for 3 months. While entire direction finder project
                    is under your supervision and under the immediate direction of the United States
                    Military Attaché at Caracas, this Government has no objection provided you
                    concur, to ultimate control of Lines’ official activities by Venezuelan
                    authorities. Please appropriately inform Lines.</p>
                <p>Appropriate United States Army officials are being informed with <pb facs="0809"
                        n="795" xml:id="pg795"/> respect to these requirements as they apply to Army
                    representatives who will proceed to Venezuela in connection with direction
                    finder project.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d659-f1" n="5" xml:id="d659-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported that Venezuela accepted a plan proposed by the United
                    States to survey and eliminate clandestine radio.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
